<TextPage
  title="Privacy"
  description="How taren.se handles your data: no accounts, no forms, no analytics, no cookies and no third-party scripts."
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy on taren.se"
  intro="Short version: this website does not ask for personal data, sets no cookies, runs no analytics and loads no third-party scripts."
  updated="2026-11-20"
>
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    taren.se is run by {SITE.founder}, an independent developer in {SITE.country}, under the name Taren. For
    questions about privacy or this website, email <ContactEmail />.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It has no user accounts, sign-up forms, newsletters or comment fields.</li>
    <li>It sets no cookies and does not use local storage for tracking.</li>
    <li>
      If you choose a language with the EN | SV switch, your browser remembers that choice in its local storage. It
      stays on your device and is never sent to Taren.
    </li>
    <li>It runs no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts.</li>
    <li>It loads no third-party scripts, fonts or embeds. Fonts and images are served from taren.se itself.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If you email Taren</h2>
  <p>
    If you send an email, your address and message are used to read and answer it. They are kept in that mailbox,
    which is provided by Microsoft’s Outlook.com service.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Cloudflare. To deliver pages and protect the site against abuse, Cloudflare necessarily
    processes technical information about each request, such as your IP address, browser user agent and the page you
    asked for. Taren does not use this information to identify or profile visitors. Cloudflare’s handling of this data
    is described in the <ExternalLink href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</ExternalLink>.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Some links lead to other services, such as <ExternalLink href={KOFI_URL}>Ko-fi</ExternalLink> for optional
    support. Those services have their own privacy policies, which apply once you are on their sites. If you
    contribute through Ko-fi, Ko-fi may share details you give it, such as your name, message and email address, with
    Taren. Taren uses them only to acknowledge and keep a record of the contribution and does not sell or share them.
  </p>

  <h2>Downloads and app updates</h2>
  <p>
    Program files and update information for Taren's Windows apps are served from downloads.taren.se, which also runs
    on Cloudflare. When you download a file, or an app checks for updates, Cloudflare processes the same kind of
    technical information as for this website (for example your IP address and the program version in the request).
    Taren does not use this information to identify or profile you.
  </p>

  <h2>Products</h2>
  <p>
    Each Windows app ships with its own privacy information (<code>PRIVACY.txt</code> next to the program). In short:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Lumen Capture</strong> has no accounts or telemetry and keeps recordings on your computer. It connects to
      the internet only for its update check (on by default, at most once a day, can be turned off), to download a
      caption model when you ask for one (from huggingface.co), and to stream to the service you set up yourself.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>PDF Studio</strong> works entirely on your computer and opens no network connections of its own.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    If you are in the EU or EEA, the GDPR gives you rights regarding personal data, including access, correction and
    deletion. Because this website does not collect personal data itself, there is usually nothing held about you
    unless you have emailed Taren or contributed through Ko-fi. To ask, email <ContactEmail />. You can also contact
    the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (IMY).
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this page changes, the date at the top will be updated.</p>
</TextPage>
